Subject: [PATCH 10846/11171] Record that the flag ledger cannot express a
 measured null

The dashboard reported 4/4 shipped-but-unevaluated an hour after an A/B
measured two of those four flags. The reason is structural, not stale data.

All 136 flags in ops/arc_flag_ledger.yaml are state unevaluated, and 15 already
carry evidence. The only transition out of unevaluated is to "on", and it fires
only when the measured arm beats baseline. A flag that is measured and found
not to help records its evidence, sets promotable false, and stays unevaluated
forever, indistinguishable from a flag nobody ever tested.

Those are different facts. One is a coverage gap and an argument to go measure.
The other is a finding and an argument to stop spending. Collapsing them hides
every negative result and makes the headline count monotone -- it can only fall
on a promotion, and fifteen measured flags have never moved it.

The r11l tools A/B is the live instance: the tool arm fired twice where it had
never fired, and levels, charged actions and efficiency were identical. A clean
null that the ledger has no way to say.

Recording a second gap alongside it: that A/B ran as a direct eval invocation
rather than through --measure, so its evidence never reached the ledger at all.

Deliberately not fixed. Adding a state changes what a headline number means,
and that is an operator call rather than something to slip into a status check.
The note states the shape a fix would take and, until then, how to read the
line honestly: it counts flags not yet promoted.

